\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 8 | 0.0057 | 0.0687 | 0.0453 | 0.0484 | 0.0217 |\n| 16 | 0.0067 | 0.0666 | 0.0523 | 0.0397 | 0.0222 |\n| 32 | 0.0111 | 0.0790 | 0.0467 | 0.0466 | 0.0228 |\n| 64 | 0.0175 | 0.0663 | 0.0529 | 0.0487 | 0.0280 |\n| 128 | 0.0299 | 0.0685 | 0.0549 | 0.0572 | 0.0416 |\n| 256 | 0.0560 | 0.0898 | 0.0796 | 0.0827 | 0.0626 |\n| 512 | 0.1063 | 0.1472 | 0.1320 | 0.1351 | 0.1153 |\n| 1,024 | 0.2040 | 0.2493 | 0.2281 | 0.2315 | 0.2051 |\n| 1,536 | 0.3003 | 0.3460 | 0.3192 | 0.3257 | 0.2926 |\n| 2,432 | 0.4693 | 0.5249 | 0.4813 | 0.4942 | 0.4449 |\n\nSmall-call medians have visible launch/scheduling noise; all variants were\nrun in separate processes. The result ordering is nevertheless consistent.\n\n## Breakdown medians (ms)\n\n| Blocks | Path | H2D | Resident decode | Total |\n|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| 256 | CD3 variable CSR | 0.0430 | 0.0228 | 0.0626 |\n| 256 | CD3 1x16 fixed | 0.0552 | 0.0373 | 0.0796 |\n| 256 | CD3 16x16 fixed | 0.0569 | 0.0376 | 0.0827 |\n| 256 | P4Flat | 0.0657 | 0.0448 | 0.0898 |\n| 256 | Raw | 0.0560 | 0 | 0.0560 |\n| 1,024 | CD3 variable CSR | 0.1507 | 0.0560 | 0.2051 |\n| 1,024 | P4Flat | 0.1858 | 0.0740 | 0.2493 |\n| 1,024 | Raw | 0.2040 | 0 | 0.2040 |\n| 2,432 | CD3 variable CSR | 0.3403 | 0.1075 | 0.4449 |\n| 2,432 | CD3 1x16 fixed | 0.3702 | 0.1223 | 0.4813 |\n| 2,432 | CD3 16x16 fixed | 0.3846 | 0.1225 | 0.4942 |\n| 2,432 | P4Flat | 0.3970 | 0.1272 | 0.5249 |\n| 2,432 | Raw | 0.4693 | 0 | 0.4693 |\n\n## Size and correctness at 256 blocks\n\n- Raw K+V transfer: 16,777,216 bytes.\n- Variable CSR K+V transfer: 11,961,880 bytes, `1.4026x` ratio and 28.7%\n  fewer bytes than raw.\n- Mean exceptions: K 266.02, V 256.27.\n- Maximum exceptions: K 576, V 1,013.\n- Raw-preferred records: K 0, V 0.\n- Bit exact: true for every measured configuration and block count.\n- An all-zero, zero-exception input was also bit-exact.\n\n## Relative result\n\n- At 256 blocks, variable CSR total is 30.3% faster than P4Flat, 21.4%\n  faster than CD3 1x16 fixed, and 24.3% faster than CD3 16x16 fixed.\n- At 1,024 blocks, it is 17.7% faster than P4Flat and essentially tied with\n  raw H2D (0.5% slower).\n- At 1,536 blocks, it becomes 2.6% faster than raw H2D.\n- At 2,432 blocks, it is 15.2% faster than P4Flat, 7.6% faster than CD3 1x16\n  fixed, 10.0% faster than CD3 16x16 fixed, and 5.2% faster than raw H2D.\n\nCPU encode timing from this prototype is not a production apples-to-apples\ncomparison: CSR encoding runs directly on the calling thread's OpenMP team,\nwhereas existing codecs use their configured background-worker affinities.\nWith a 1,020-entry scratch the CSR path needs one encode pass on this sample;\nthe remaining added CPU work is compact-arena assembly.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /home/ubuntu/CD3_VARIABLE_KV_CSR_REPORT_20260904.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788519979565,"completed_at_ms":1788519979566}}
